# Crew 4 and "whenever this Vehicle ... attacks": turn 1 Bot1 casts Lumbering Worldwagon (a Black Lotus) and then one Guerrilla Gorilla (power 2): the Gorilla alone
# cannot crew it (total power 2 is under 4 - the refusal). Turn 3 a second Guerrilla Gorilla makes four, and the two crew it (the positive control). It attacks
# as a creature whose power is the number of lands: three lands (the Forest, the one its enters trigger found, and turn 3's Forest) when crewed, then four
# when the attack trigger finds another, so it deals 4 to Bot2, who is at 16. (The Mox is an artifact, not a land, and Bot2's Island is not Bot1's: power 4, not 5.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Lumbering Worldwagon
Guerrilla Gorilla
Guerrilla Gorilla
Forest
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Lumbering Worldwagon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Search(Forest)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Battlefield.Lumbering Worldwagon.Activate(Ability: Crew)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Lumbering Worldwagon.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Lumbering Worldwagon > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Search(Forest)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield.Lumbering Worldwagon.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Lumbering Worldwagon.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Lumbering Worldwagon.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla#2.Tapped = true
